# Nagar Shield — Edge Function environment
#
# These are **server-side** variables. They are set per function with
# `supabase secrets set`, never as a project-wide default — a project-wide
# default is readable by every future function, including one that is added
# by mistake.
#
# The service-role key is the only credential any function holds beyond the
# project URL. It crosses the RLS boundary by design: the jobs delete Storage
# objects, scrub PII on rows no client may read, and write `job_runs`.
#
# This file lists the variable **names** with placeholders and no real
# values. The real local values live in `.env.local`, which is gitignored.
# See `docs/operations/secrets.md`.

# The project URL. Supabase injects this into every function automatically,
# so it is listed for completeness rather than for setting.
SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon (publishable) key. Not needed by the job functions — they use
# the service role — but the client-facing functions need it to resolve the
# caller's session.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The service-role key. Server-side only. Never in an EAS profile, never in
# a Vercel environment variable, never in a client-facing .env.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# The allowlisted reverse-geocoder.
#
# There is no user-supplied host — that is the SSRF closure. The local
# default points at the public Nominatim instance; CI points it at a stub.
GEOCODE_BASE_URL=https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The mail transport — the password-reset code.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The `password-reset` function mails a 6-digit code the user types. GoTrue's
# own mailer cannot carry it: its recovery template renders a **link**, and
# the code appears nowhere in the message it sends.
#
# **Exactly one** of these is set. There is no fallback — a deployment with
# neither cannot send a code, and the function says so rather than pretending
# the code was delivered.
#
#   MAIL_SMTP_URL       — the production path. A transactional-mail relay,
#                         e.g. smtps://user:pass@smtp.example.com:465
#   MAIL_HTTP_ENDPOINT  — a mailpit-compatible HTTP API. The local stack's
#                         choice: the SMTP port is container-internal and the
#                         Edge Function runs on the host, but mailpit's HTTP
#                         API is published on 54324.
#
# The envelope sender. A real domain, so the message is not filed as spam.
MAIL_FROM=no-reply@nagarshield.bd
